1
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:45,620
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 6=

2
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:48,150
How could the killer
bring himself to take

3
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:49,980
a hammer to such a lovable dog?

4
00:00:51,470 --> 00:00:52,880
Isn't everything we're doing

5
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:54,840
to get justice for it?

6
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:58,560
He had us come out this late.

7
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:00,560
We won't come up empty-handed, will we?

8
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:05,950
You're Chen, right?

9
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:07,040
This is our Captain Qin.

10
00:01:07,710 --> 00:01:08,180
Hello.

11
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:08,840
Captain Qin.

12
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:09,640
Sorry to trouble you.

13
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:10,510
It's fine.

14
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:11,840
Tell us what you know.

15
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,070
Jin Juan was quite
an interesting young woman.

16
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:15,760
She'd been renting
this place for over six months.

17
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:19,590
She did all the renovations herself.

18
00:01:19,790 --> 00:01:20,590
She lived alone.

19
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:21,710
Sometimes she wouldn't come home.

20
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:23,350
She didn't talk much,

21
00:01:23,350 --> 00:01:25,070
but she always paid her rent on time.

22
00:01:26,230 --> 00:01:27,000
All right.

23
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,230
We'll go upstairs and take a look.

24
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:30,400
Sure.

25
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:36,420
(Unit 2)

26
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:02,840
Li.

27
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:04,710
Sorry.

28
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:08,310
I think we contaminated the scene.

29
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:10,910
What do we do now?

30
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,360
In a moment,

31
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,710
go back exactly

32
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,430
the way you came.

33
00:02:17,910 --> 00:02:18,710
Keep going.

34
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:19,470
I...

35
00:02:33,190 --> 00:02:34,000
Captain Qin.

36
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:36,190
I found two footprints on the chair.

37
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:38,000
The toes are pointing toward the window.

38
00:02:38,190 --> 00:02:40,400
The victim must have
stepped onto this chair

39
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,400
and climbed up to the window,

40
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:42,840
then fell to her death.

41
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:46,520
Check first

42
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:48,520
if you have a photo
of the victim's shoes.

43
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,520
Let me see.

44
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:53,190
Keep your voice down.

45
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:04,190
Found it.

46
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:13,590
Captain Qin.

47
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,840
The tread pattern
matches the victim's shoes.

48
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:21,630
There are finger marks on the window.

49
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:24,800
Some are newer than others.

50
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:25,710
I can't tell them apart.

51
00:03:26,150 --> 00:03:27,240
Come out first.

52
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:29,360
Call the trace evidence team right away.

53
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:31,150
Have them send someone over

54
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,430
to process the scene.

55
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:47,120
From now on, you can't

56
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:49,080
take everything I say at face value.

57
00:03:50,910 --> 00:03:51,680
Move.

58
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:52,470
You're stepping on my foot.

59
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:53,560
Sorry.

60
00:03:54,140 --> 00:04:01,420
(Rainy Night Hammer Killer Case.
White-Haired Female Corpse Case)

61
00:04:01,430 --> 00:04:02,360
Ming.

62
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:04,960
I've got a lot of things over there
that still need sorting out.

63
00:04:05,150 --> 00:04:07,520
Why did you call me here to look at

64
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,430
these unsolved cases?

65
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:10,750
I'm taking a roundabout approach.

66
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:14,360
Maybe if we study
these two cases more closely,

67
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,560
we'll find a lead
in the Riverside Skeleton Case.

68
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:19,240
If only it were that simple.

69
00:04:19,510 --> 00:04:21,750
There's no basis
for linking these cases.

70
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:22,720
Then tell me,

71
00:04:23,510 --> 00:04:25,070
after 30 years,

72
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:26,870
why haven't they found
a single viable suspect in either case?

73
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:29,870
Look at the photos
taken before the victim's autopsy.

74
00:04:30,430 --> 00:04:32,510
Aside from the bra clasp
broken during the fall,

75
00:04:32,830 --> 00:04:34,310
the victim's clothes
were all neat and tidy.

76
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:35,870
She was dressed
as if she were going out.

77
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:37,560
But her shoes

78
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:39,040
had very clean soles.

79
00:04:39,510 --> 00:04:40,830
So what's your theory?

80
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,070
I suspect

81
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:44,750
Jin Juan didn't fall

82
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:46,720
from her own home,

83
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,920
as the case file says,

84
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:49,560
but somewhere else.

85
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:11,040
Isn't this a certificate you need
before getting married?

86
00:05:11,510 --> 00:05:12,390
What's going on?

87
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:14,070
Zhang Zhiqiang and Jin Juan
were planning to get married?

88
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,800
Wasn't she Huo Qicheng's wife?

89
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,680
Who's Zhang Zhiqiang?

90
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:21,600
Was he that pretty boy

91
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,830
we saw at the club that day?

92
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:24,560
I'm telling you,

93
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,070
there's definitely more to
Jin Juan than meets the eye.

94
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:31,360
You can't judge people
or things by appearances.

95
00:05:32,270 --> 00:05:35,270
Go check the room right now.

96
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:36,950
See if there are any men's belongings.

97
00:05:37,270 --> 00:05:38,070
Hurry.

98
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:38,870
Okay.

99
00:05:53,270 --> 00:05:54,270
I've checked everywhere.

100
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:55,680
There's only one cup in the bathroom,

101
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,190
one toothbrush, and one towel.

102
00:05:57,270 --> 00:05:59,240
There are only women's clothes
on the balcony too.

103
00:06:01,630 --> 00:06:02,630
So that means

104
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:05,360
apart from that
marital status certificate,

105
00:06:06,070 --> 00:06:07,510
there's nothing in this apartment

106
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:10,480
to suggest that a man ever lived here.

107
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:13,270
Jin Juan had a huge villa
she could live in,

108
00:06:13,270 --> 00:06:15,270
yet she chose to stay
in this shabby little apartment.

109
00:06:15,310 --> 00:06:16,190
Why?

110
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:17,950
Could this be a devoted woman

111
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:18,950
who fell for a heartless man?

112
00:06:20,870 --> 00:06:22,630
Why don't we meet this Zhang Zhiqiang?

113
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,800
It's all documented in the file.

114
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,040
(Rainy Night Hammer Killer Case.
White-Haired Female Corpse Case)

115
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:29,870
Two footprints were found
on a stool by the window.

116
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:30,920
After comparison,

117
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,040
the footprints
were confirmed to be Jin Juan's.

118
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:34,510
They were definitely her footprints.

119
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:35,920
But the question is,

120
00:06:36,390 --> 00:06:37,800
why were both her feet

121
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,360
planted fully on the stool?

122
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:44,240
If she was only using the stool

123
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:46,830
as a step to jump from the window,

124
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,830
she only needed
to put one foot on the stool.

125
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:51,070
Her other foot could have
stepped straight onto the windowsill.

126
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:54,070
This looks more like...

127
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:57,950
You mean she was changing
her shoes in a hurry to go out.

128
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,390
She stood on the stool
with both feet while tying her shoelaces,

129
00:07:00,630 --> 00:07:02,600
leaving two complete footprints.

130
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:04,800
Exactly.

131
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
The autopsy records from that year

132
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,310
also raised several key questions.

133
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:09,310
First,

134
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:12,390
the proximal joint of the victim's
right middle finger was dislocated,

135
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:13,950
but there was no fracture.

136
00:07:14,510 --> 00:07:15,720
Only a force applied sideways

137
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:17,600
could cause this kind
of isolated dislocation.

138
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:19,630
But in a fall from a height,

139
00:07:19,870 --> 00:07:21,750
the force on the fingers
would be longitudinal,

140
00:07:21,750 --> 00:07:23,120
which wouldn't
cause this kind of injury.

141
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:23,720
Second,

142
00:07:24,870 --> 00:07:26,480
the palms of both the victim's hands

143
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:29,120
showed regularly
spaced vertical abrasions.

144
00:07:29,270 --> 00:07:30,310
Marks like these

145
00:07:30,630 --> 00:07:33,160
could only form if both hands
were gripping tightly

146
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:35,510
an object with evenly
spaced vertical ridges

147
00:07:35,510 --> 00:07:36,480
on its surface.

148
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:37,600
Third,

149
00:07:38,390 --> 00:07:39,750
there were small patches
of subcutaneous bleeding

150
00:07:40,070 --> 00:07:42,120
on the inner sides of both ankles.

151
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:45,240
These were caused
by something smooth and flexible,

152
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:48,040
such as being gripped
by someone's hands.

153
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:50,360
And since both inner ankles
were injured at the same time,

154
00:07:50,390 --> 00:07:52,000
those injuries couldn't
have been caused by the fall.

155
00:07:54,430 --> 00:07:55,270
In other words,

156
00:07:55,510 --> 00:07:57,560
someone grabbed her ankles
while she was high above the ground.

157
00:07:57,830 --> 00:07:59,240
She desperately tried to hold on

158
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:01,430
to something with a threaded
surface to save herself.

159
00:08:01,630 --> 00:08:02,630
But when her strength gave out,

160
00:08:03,190 --> 00:08:05,430
she lost her grip and fell to her death.

161
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,600
Interesting.

162
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:13,070
Maybe we can solve
this cold case along the way.

163
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:14,830
Section Chief Qin.

164
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:17,190
Next time you perform an autopsy,

165
00:08:17,270 --> 00:08:19,920
even if you determine
the killer was an alien,

166
00:08:20,390 --> 00:08:21,480
I'd still have to check

167
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:23,390
whether any UFOs
had been spotted recently.

168
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,390
You're indulging him a little too much.

169
00:08:26,390 --> 00:08:27,360
Deputy Captain Lin.

170
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:31,120
If we approach this
from what we know now

171
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:33,000
and reconstruct the crime scene,

172
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:35,550
we might be able to recover some details

173
00:08:35,550 --> 00:08:36,550
that were overlooked back then.

174
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,030
If the location of the fall

175
00:08:40,030 --> 00:08:42,240
wasn't where the case file indicated,

176
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:43,670
then where was it?

177
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:51,980
(Jin Juan)

178
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:54,270
Captain Qin.

179
00:08:55,630 --> 00:08:56,720
Have some food.

180
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:58,960
The cafeteria made chicken legs today.

181
00:09:00,670 --> 00:09:01,670
You go ahead.

182
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,270
Captain Qin.

183
00:09:08,790 --> 00:09:09,790
We've brought Zhang Zhiqiang in.

184
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:13,000
Zhang Zhiqiang, 35 years old.

185
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,440
He's from Zhangjia Village
on the outskirts of the city.

186
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:15,750
Middle school education, unmarried.

187
00:09:15,750 --> 00:09:17,270
His record is clean.
No prior convictions.

188
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,390
What's his relationship with Jin Juan?

189
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:25,000
Jin Juan was also from Zhangjia Village.

190
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,750
They were from the same village
and knew each other from childhood.

191
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,200
Childhood friends?

192
00:09:28,910 --> 00:09:30,440
Before Jin Juan left Zhangjia Village,

193
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,080
their families
had even discussed marriage.

194
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:34,120
Later, Jin Juan married Huo Qicheng.

195
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:36,630
Zhang Zhiqiang now runs
a solid wood furniture store.

196
00:09:36,790 --> 00:09:37,960
He also has a younger sister

197
00:09:38,030 --> 00:09:39,000
named Zhang Tiantian.

198
00:09:39,150 --> 00:09:39,960
Zhang Tiantian?

199
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:45,100
(Permanent Resident Registration Form:
Zhang Tiantian)

200
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,550
She's that girl

201
00:09:49,550 --> 00:09:50,440
with the red motorcycle, right?

202
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,270
Right.

203
00:09:51,510 --> 00:09:52,550
That all lines up.

204
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,550
Let's go talk to Zhang Zhiqiang.

205
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:58,270
You're not eating?

206
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:14,000
Officer, what happened to Jin Juan?

207
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
(Leniency for Confession,
Severity for Resistance)

208
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,240
You're Zhang Zhiqiang, right?

209
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:18,870
What's your relationship with Jin Juan?

210
00:10:19,510 --> 00:10:21,000
Before she left Zhangjia Village,

211
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:22,200
we dated.

212
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:23,510
You dated?

213
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,600
How serious did it get?

214
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:26,960
Did you ever talk about marriage?

215
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:27,910
No.

216
00:10:27,910 --> 00:10:28,910
(Jin Juan's Childhood Sweetheart:
Zhang Zhiqiang)

217
00:10:28,910 --> 00:10:29,840
She got married.

218
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,600
When was the last time

219
00:10:33,510 --> 00:10:34,360
you saw Jin Juan?

220
00:10:43,980 --> 00:10:45,500
(Certificate of Unmarried Status)

221
00:10:45,510 --> 00:10:46,480
Remember now?

222
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:49,080
Answer me.

223
00:10:49,870 --> 00:10:51,270
When did you last see her?

224
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:54,270
A week ago.

225
00:10:54,750 --> 00:10:56,240
We grew up together.

226
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:57,390
Her family was poor when she was young.

227
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:58,870
She started working at an early age.

228
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,000
I learned carpentry

229
00:11:00,270 --> 00:11:01,550
and came to the city too.

230
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:03,030
We were supposed

231
00:11:04,390 --> 00:11:06,080
to be together.

232
00:11:07,150 --> 00:11:09,270
Then how did she end up
marrying Huo Qicheng?

233
00:11:09,270 --> 00:11:10,670
Huo was a businessman.

234
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:13,270
He was the head
of an urban construction company.

235
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:14,960
He was a shameless man.

236
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:16,600
Jin Juan was singing
at a dance hall back then.

237
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,550
She was beautiful.

238
00:11:17,670 --> 00:11:19,270
Huo took a liking to her right away.

239
00:11:19,270 --> 00:11:20,390
He was constantly hanging around her

240
00:11:20,390 --> 00:11:21,750
and shamelessly pursuing her.

241
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:25,440
Jin Juan loved me. I know she did.

242
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,270
But there was nothing she could do.

243
00:11:26,630 --> 00:11:28,150
Her father was sick at the time,

244
00:11:28,150 --> 00:11:29,120
and her younger brother
still had to go to school.

245
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:30,150
What else could she do?

246
00:11:30,150 --> 00:11:31,320
There was nothing I could do either.

247
00:11:33,390 --> 00:11:34,600
She had no choice but to leave me.

248
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:38,840
I thought the two of them
were doing pretty well.

249
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,910
Until I ran into her
on the street again.

250
00:12:16,670 --> 00:12:17,550
It's you.

251
00:12:27,030 --> 00:12:28,390
Your water pipe is broken, right?

252
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:31,270
The hotel sent me.

253
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,200
How long have you been doing this?

254
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:37,720
I've been doing it all along.

255
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,720
Have you been doing well?

256
00:12:46,670 --> 00:12:47,510
Pretty well.

257
00:12:51,300 --> 00:12:52,940
(Estazolam)
Sleeping pills.

258
00:12:54,630 --> 00:12:55,720
Try not to take too many.

259
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,510
They're not good for you.

260
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:03,840
I thought Jin Juan
was living a good life.

261
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,390
But Huo Qicheng
was out partying all the time,

262
00:13:06,670 --> 00:13:07,910
so she had no choice but to move out.

263
00:13:08,670 --> 00:13:09,840
How could I stand by

264
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:12,390
when she was so unhappy?

265
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:15,240
Of course I still
had feelings for Jin Juan.

266
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:21,390
Leave him.

267
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:23,390
Don't say that.

268
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:27,630
Jin Juan.

269
00:13:28,910 --> 00:13:30,750
I want you to have a good life.

270
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:35,510
You deserve more love.

271
00:13:43,550 --> 00:13:45,360
You've kept it all these years.

272
00:13:45,390 --> 00:13:46,720
It'd be a shame to throw it away.

273
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:50,510
Juan.

274
00:13:51,910 --> 00:13:52,960
I want to marry you.

275
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:56,870
I have a trade.

276
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,150
I can make enough to support you.

277
00:14:02,510 --> 00:14:03,750
Do you really want to marry me?

278
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:20,030
After that, we got back together.

279
00:14:21,790 --> 00:14:23,200
Jin Juan wanted to help me.

280
00:14:24,270 --> 00:14:26,200
I opened a solid wood furniture store.

281
00:14:26,790 --> 00:14:29,440
She often referred people
to my store for custom furniture.

282
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:32,910
When business was slow for a while,

283
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:36,670
she asked me to work
at the urban construction company.

284
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,630
She said I'd have a stable job there.

285
00:14:39,550 --> 00:14:40,870
How could I possibly go?

286
00:14:42,150 --> 00:14:45,080
Luckily, Jin Juan
didn't pressure me after that.

287
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:48,600
Instead, she gave my sister money

288
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:50,000
to open a clothing store,

289
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:51,960
and even bought her a motorcycle.

290
00:14:52,550 --> 00:14:55,960
She said it was so
Tiantian could support herself.

291
00:14:56,910 --> 00:14:58,480
But deep down, I knew.

292
00:14:59,150 --> 00:15:02,120
I knew she did all that for me.

293
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:08,900
(Application for Certificate
of Marital Status: Zhang Zhiqiang)

294
00:15:11,670 --> 00:15:12,480
Later,

295
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,840
Huo died.

296
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:17,360
I thought it was perfect timing.

297
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:19,480
We could finally be together

298
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:20,360
openly.

299
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:25,270
Juan.

300
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:27,120
I've got everything ready.

301
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:29,750
(Certificate of Unmarried Status)
We can finally be together.

302
00:15:34,270 --> 00:15:35,080
Zhiqiang.

303
00:15:36,750 --> 00:15:38,670
I asked you here today
because I want to break up.

304
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:42,790
Why?

305
00:15:45,150 --> 00:15:46,510
Is it because of that guy at the club?

306
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:48,320
Didn't you say you brought him there

307
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,870
just to put on an act for the police?

308
00:15:52,750 --> 00:15:53,600
No.

309
00:15:55,150 --> 00:15:56,510
It has nothing to do with him.

310
00:15:58,030 --> 00:15:59,200
Then why are you breaking up with me?

311
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:01,550
Huo is already dead.

312
00:16:01,550 --> 00:16:03,200
There's nothing
standing between us anymore.

313
00:16:03,790 --> 00:16:05,240
Huo Qicheng is dead,

314
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:09,200
but things aren't that simple.

315
00:16:09,550 --> 00:16:10,600
You have no idea

316
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:12,600
how many shady things
he was involved in.

317
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:18,150
The police have been coming
to see me from time to time.

318
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:21,200
I... I don't want to drag you into this.

319
00:16:23,030 --> 00:16:23,510
Then...

320
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,320
Then let's go somewhere else

321
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:28,600
and start over, okay?

322
00:16:28,670 --> 00:16:30,320
You don't understand.

323
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:32,320
You don't understand.

324
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:35,440
Things aren't as simple as you think.

325
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:37,360
I can't distance myself from all this.

326
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,240
I can't get away from it.

327
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:43,390
I don't want to drag you into it.

328
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:50,510
Zhang Zhiqiang.

329
00:16:53,150 --> 00:16:53,960
We're breaking up.

330
00:16:56,030 --> 00:16:57,390
I won't agree to that!

331
00:16:59,670 --> 00:17:00,480
Juan.

332
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:02,750
If you don't agree, I'll jump from here.

333
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,510
Now that Huo is dead,

334
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,550
you want to break up with me?

335
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,400
Are you serious?

336
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:20,680
Yes.

337
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:24,400
I'm serious.

338
00:17:30,030 --> 00:17:30,830
Fine.

339
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:34,200
I'm leaving.

340
00:17:49,310 --> 00:17:50,160
I'm leaving.

341
00:17:51,510 --> 00:17:52,310
Come down.

342
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:57,790
You're too high up.

343
00:17:59,590 --> 00:18:00,400
It's dangerous.

344
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,110
Do you believe me?

345
00:18:12,590 --> 00:18:14,510
When you care deeply about someone,

346
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,200
you can sense when something's wrong.

347
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:19,240
After I left her place that day,

348
00:18:20,110 --> 00:18:22,000
my right eyelid wouldn't stop twitching.

349
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:24,640
It felt like a huge weight
was pressing on my chest.

350
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:26,030
I didn't sleep a wink all night.

351
00:18:26,790 --> 00:18:28,920
Jin Juan was in such a hurry
to make me leave.

352
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:31,510
She must have been worried
something would happen.

353
00:18:31,790 --> 00:18:33,200
She didn't want to drag me into it.

354
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,680
Officer, what exactly happened?

355
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:38,350
Nothing serious.

356
00:18:39,310 --> 00:18:40,110
Go on.

357
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:42,240
How could it be nothing?

358
00:18:42,310 --> 00:18:43,640
Why bring me here if nothing happened?

359
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:49,160
Calm down first.

360
00:18:50,310 --> 00:18:51,240
Something

361
00:18:55,110 --> 00:18:55,960
happened to Jin Juan.

362
00:18:59,790 --> 00:19:00,590
Zhang Zhiqiang.

363
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:03,350
Can you think back carefully

364
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:07,070
to everything you remember

365
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:10,960
before you left Jin Juan's place?

366
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:13,480
Where things were placed in the room,

367
00:19:14,830 --> 00:19:15,880
whether the window was closed

368
00:19:17,070 --> 00:19:18,200
or open,

369
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:20,440
where the chair was,

370
00:19:21,790 --> 00:19:23,640
what Jin Juan was wearing,

371
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:26,830
and when you left,

372
00:19:29,070 --> 00:19:30,160
whether you ran into anyone.

373
00:19:31,550 --> 00:19:32,720
Tell us

374
00:19:33,550 --> 00:19:34,680
anything you can remember,

375
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,240
okay?

376
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:46,680
That day,

377
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:49,480
I ran into an aggressive man
dressed in black.

378
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,480
If something happened to Jin Juan,

379
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:53,510
he must have done it.

380
00:20:12,260 --> 00:20:16,780
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

381
00:20:19,850 --> 00:20:24,630
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

382
00:20:27,340 --> 00:20:32,720
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

383
00:20:33,250 --> 00:20:38,580
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

384
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:48,570
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

385
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:54,250
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

386
00:20:56,290 --> 00:21:04,600
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

387
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:10,450
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

388
00:21:11,910 --> 00:21:20,030
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

389
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:25,760
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

390
00:21:27,540 --> 00:21:35,580
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

391
00:21:35,860 --> 00:21:43,130
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

392
00:21:43,330 --> 00:21:47,740
♪Can you hear me?♪

393
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:51,540
♪Can you hear me?♪

394
00:21:51,540 --> 00:21:59,000
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

395
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:06,740
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

396
00:22:07,070 --> 00:22:12,680
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

397
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:18,160
♪After all these years♪

398
00:22:20,670 --> 00:22:28,150
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

399
00:22:29,050 --> 00:22:30,350
♪And tell you♪

400
00:22:31,570 --> 00:22:34,840
♪I haven't let you down♪
